<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000030> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A generically dependent continuant that is about some thing." .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000030> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000030> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "ICEs are abstract entities that convey information about things in the world. ICEs represent the information encoded in physical artifacts such as photographs, books, or digital storage medium (as opposed to the physical medium itself).  A particular ICE can be encoded simultaneously in many physical or digital mediums and formats. For example, only one instance of the first edition of \"War and Peace\" exists as an ICE, representing information conveyed in this work. But many instances of \"War and Peace\" exist at the level of their physical concretizations in printed books or digital devices." .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000030> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Pier: 'data, information or knowledge'. OR 'representation" .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000030> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "information content entity"@en .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000030> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "information" .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000030> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000031> .
